steam-arm-setup (2.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Renderer check: handler logs whether title draws on GPU or on CPU
    (llvmpipe); STEAM_ARM_RENDERER_CHECK=0 turns it off.
  * Page size in settings menu title bar and in setup and removal banners.
  * FEX build matches CPU: fex-emu-armv8.0, -armv8.2 or -armv8.4; setup
    on ARMv8.0 CPUs (Cortex-A72) no longer stops.
  * Display mode restore after titles and when Steam closes;
    STEAM_ARM_MODE_RESTORE=0 turns it off.
  * steam-arm --shutdown, with SIGTERM fallback; interface switch uses it.
  * MangoHud in 64-bit x86 Linux titles: library copied from root
    filesystem into client folder and preloaded from there.
  * kde-input-prompt component, off by default; profile key multiblock.
  * Compatibility tool and GoldSrc log lines; Information shows OpenGL
    and CPU governor per cluster.
  * Restore keeps Proton choice made now. Menu: restore summary button
    Next; wizard Back no longer skips Vulkan screen.
  * Launcher keeps host Bluetooth adapter on: writes adapter state to
    System/Bluetooth/Enabled in config.vdf, powers it on at exit when
    client left it off.
  * Armv8.1 check: setup and launcher stop on CPUs without LSE atomics
    (steam-for-linux #13288); STEAM_ARM_ALLOW_ARMV80=1 skips it.
  * First start: desktop notification reports client download; menu
    icons show plain disc until client's own icon file arrives.
  * FEX version read from FEXGetConfig --version (FEX-2608 and newer
    have no FEXInterpreter).
  * steam:// links open in Steam ARM (x-scheme-handler/steam). Update /
    Repair asks Run / Back first; kde-input-prompt label fits checklist.
  * Setup started from folder game user cannot enter (/root) no longer
    stops with "client program missing after unpacking".

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

steam-arm-setup (2.0) stable; urgency=low

  * Graphics route per title, automatic: Java and 32-bit Vulkan titles
    on Mali drivers inside emulation, others on forwarding; gfx=a|b.
  * gpu-in-emulation component, on by default on Mali GPUs: x86-64 and
    i386 Mesa with Panfrost and PanVK in second root filesystem tree.
    Driver archive checked by SHA-256.
  * GPU family detection sets component defaults; GPU_FAMILY=id by hand.
  * PhysX install step skipped: has-run value written into title's Proton
    prefix; stuck PhysX installer gets SIGTERM after 60 seconds.
  * Uninstaller: --remove, --remove --purge. Client folder kept unless
    confirmed; Valve's FEX tool files restored.
  * Other variant of this installer retired cleanly with --replace-other;
    its files kept in two backup tarballs (system, account).
  * Controller rules from Valve's steam-devices plus pads it lacks.
  * glx-lax rebuilt by apt hook after Mesa upgrades; launcher falls back
    to system GLX when copy is missing.
  * FEX tool 2609 and later: no ThunksDB path edit. FEX logging off.
  * Client downloads from stable ARM64 channel; publicbeta no longer set.
  * Fixed: second arm64 overlay layer registration hung Vulkan titles;
    GLX copy and Vulkan layer enabled only when selected; sudo rule only
    with pad-xbox; account creation without render group; re-login note.

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000

steam-arm-setup (1.2) stable; urgency=low

  * Launcher frees memory Steam overlay holds in /dev/shm after game
    sessions (two 25 MB buffers per session, kept mapped by web helper).
  * 32-bit titles: -vulkan and -force-vulkan removed (Vulkan forwarding is
    64-bit only); profile key vk32=keep keeps them.
  * Profile key gl32=off: title not detected as 64-bit runs on emulated x86
    Mesa instead of forwarded host Mesa.
  * Start scripts (hl2.sh style) followed to binary they start; 64-bit
    build preferred in arch-switch scripts, crash helpers skipped.
  * Profile args counted by Unity and Godot renderer rules.
  * Source 2 titles logged; component dialog (zenity) with no controlling
    terminal in desktop session. RESEARCH.md added.

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

steam-arm-setup (1.1) stable; urgency=low

  * Check page size before installing anything; stop on 16K or 64K kernel
    with fix for that system. STEAM_ARM_IGNORE_PAGESIZE=1 skips check.
  * New page-size component: on Raspberry Pi, select firmware's 4K page
    kernel in config.txt, keep backup, ask for reboot and second run.
  * New desktop-mode component: menu entry and desktop icon for desktop
    interface. Power menu Switch to Desktop restarts client there.
  * Menu icons from client's own icon in project banner colours; tray
    helper started by launcher.
  * Desktop icons and tray icon are separate components: icon-bigpicture,
    icon-desktop, tray. Installed games, sign-in and settings are kept.
  * Launch handler run by Valve's FEX tool: Steam overlay and MangoHud in
    x86 titles, Godot 4 on OpenGL, title profiles in /etc/steam-arm.
  * Handler engine rules for Unity: Vulkan renderer where player carries
    it, GL 4.5 report otherwise, overlay off for 32-bit players.
  * Direct3D 8 titles under Proton use DXVK (PROTON_DXVK_D3D8=1).
  * Launcher clears shared-memory segments no process maps; after many
    game sessions they filled /dev/shm and every title failed to start.
    Overlay segments steamwebhelper still maps are reclaimed at client
    restart.
  * Installer published as plain script steam-arm-install.sh; package still
    builds with build-deb.sh.
  * Icons drawn during first start once client has downloaded its icon
    file; KDE menu cache refreshes after.
  * Saved GAMEUSER naming absent account is ignored with warning instead
    of creating that account.
  * Fixed: CPU rendering after fresh install, overlay UI crash, missing
    title bar until next login.

 -- Scrumpper <Scrumpper@users.noreply.github.com>  Mon, 28 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000

